      "HOWTO and LTC commands run only the component test file; they do not provide the expected e2e command path described in PLAN.md KIT readiness.",
      "Docs are operationally usable, but they describe acceptance strength that the emitted test assets do not actually deliver."
    ]
  },
  "promotion_fit": {
    "status": "partial",
    "notes": [
      "The code is structurally promotable in the sense that it is organized under the correct REQ-004 frontend slice path and preserves the intended POST /documents business contract.",
      "Dual runtime configuration is handled via environment-based adapter wiring rather than divergent local-only architecture, which is promotable.",
      "The larger promotion issue is architectural alignment: the plan explicitly assigns shared frontend modules for API/auth/UI reuse, but this candidate keeps those concerns local to the slice.",
      "The page also creates its own QueryClient provider instead of showing how it fits a canonical app shell, so repository promotion would still need integration work."
    ]
  },
  "shared_common_assessment": {
    "status": "weak",
    "notes": [
      "The candidate does not introduce unnecessary shared extraction, which is good.",
      "However, the plan for REQ-004 explicitly expects extension of frontend.app.shared.api, frontend.app.shared.auth, and frontend.app.shared.ui. That alignment is absent.",
